course: dictionary
lesson: 2923
title: Big changes and showy feelings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Dramatically» is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. When something changes dramatically, it changes very much, and often suddenly. «The temperature dropped dramatically» tells you to expect a big difference in the numbers, not a small wobble.
explain: The second meaning is about acting. «She sighed dramatically and clutched her forehead.» A person who sighs dramatically is showing off her feelings in a big, showy way, like an actor on stage. The words around it tell you that she is performing.
explain: Use the phrases to remember it: «rise dramatically», «fall dramatically», «sigh dramatically». Ask yourself: is there a big change in the numbers, or a big show of feeling? Then swap in a simpler phrase, such as very much or in a showy way, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Dramatically is an adverb, and it describes how something happens.
fact: «Dramatically» means very much and often suddenly, as in «rise dramatically».
fact: «Dramatically» can also mean in a big, showy way, as in «sigh dramatically».
fact: Dramatic is the adjective, meaning relating to drama or plays; add -ally to make the adverb dramatically.
fact: Words ending in -ic add -ally, like basic and basically; «publicly» is the famous exception.
exercise: «The temperature dropped dramatically overnight.» What does dramatically tell you? | *A big, often sudden change | A change in who is in charge | A change in the colour of the sky | A small, slow change
exercise: «She sighed dramatically and clutched her forehead.» What does dramatically show? | *She is showing big, showy feelings | She is fast asleep | She is counting her steps | She is cold
exercise: Which word is the correct spelling of the adverb from dramatic? | dramaticaly | dramaticly | dramatickly | *dramatically
test: «Prices rose dramatically in the summer.» What does dramatically mean here? | Politely and calmly | Slowly and quietly | Only just | *Very much and often suddenly
test: Which phrase shows showy feelings? | *He groaned dramatically and fell to the floor | The lake grew dramatically | The rain rose dramatically | The number fell dramatically
exam: «The crowd cheered dramatically as the hero walked on stage.» What does dramatically mean? | Very slowly | Only just | *In a big, showy way, like an actor | Quietly and calmly
